Hi,

I=20had=20earlier=20e-mailed=20about=20an=20apparent=20NCQ=20vs=20non-NCQ=
=20command=20issue
on=20this=20machine=20in=20mvsas/libsas=20that=20didn't=20get=20any=20att=
ention
(http://kerneltrap.org/mailarchive/linux-scsi/2010/1/24/6725113),=20but
now=20I've=20run=20into=20a=20crash/panic=20issue=20as=20well...=20perhap=
s=20related=20which
is=20why=20I=20mention=20it.

Unfortunately=20I=20don't=20have=20a=20full=20backtrace,=20but=20I'm=20go=
ing=20to=20try=20to
reproduce=20it=20tonight=20with=20netconsole=20set=20up.

Attached=20is=20a=20screenshot=20of=20the=20crash;=20the=20visible=20part=
=20of=20the=20trace
goes=20something=20like

mvs_interrupt
mvs_64xx_isr
mvs_int_full
mvs_int_rx
scsi_io_completion
mvs_slot_compete
sas_ata_task_done
ata_qc_complete
__ata_qc_complete
ata_sg_clean
swiotlb_unmap_sg_attrs
...=20and=20then=20it=20cuts=20off.

After=20this=20the=20machine=20was=20completely=20unresponsive,=20didn't=
=20even=20ping.
Please=20let=20me=20know=20if=20you=20have=20any=20ideas=20for=20figuring=
=20out=20what's=20wrong
here,=20if=20there's=20something=20I=20should=20test,=20etc.=20I=20notice=
d=20that=20there
were=20a=20bunch=20of=20patches=20a=20few=20months=20ago=20for=20mvsas,=
=20but=20they=20were
never=20merged...=20should=20I=20try=20those?=20I=20checked=20the=20commi=
ts=20that=20went
into=202.6.33,=20that=20didn't=20seem=20to=20have=20any=20relevant=20chan=
ges=20to=20mvsas,
libsas,=20or=20libata=20core=20features,=20but=20I=20can=20try=20that=20t=
oo=20if=20you=20think
it's=20likely=20to=20help=20things=20out.

The=20workload=20that=20triggered=20this=20was=20just=20dd=20reading=20an=
d=20writing
(simultaneously)=20to=2011=20of=20the=20disks=20(/dev/zero=20->=20disk,=
=20disk=20->
/dev/null,=20bs=3D1M).

Some=20information=20about=20the=20machine:

Supermicro=20X8DTE,=202x=20L5520=20cpu,=2024G=20ram=20(12G=20per=20cpu).=
=20Areca=201300ix-16
controller,=20with=2012=20drives=20attached.

Various=20virtualization=20features=20enabled=20in=20bios,=20like=20VT-d,=
=20SR-IOV,
etc=20(none=20of=20which=20I'm=20using,=20but=20wanted=20to=20play=20with=
=20at=20some=20point).
